Hi [~accountid:6078612fb5dffc006f5413c9] 

  

Regarding the repayment of  mechanics’s wages, please see below in red advice from external counsel: 

{color:#ff5630}The repayment clause in the contract is as such not an issue if the 3PL is solely responsible to fulfil all employer obligations as the employer of the 3PL employees, such as not limited to: salary payments and administration, statutory detections, maintaining records, monitoring attendance, handling grievances and disciplinary issues, termination of employment, etc. {color}

{color:#ff5630}The Repayment of salaries of the 3PL is therefore possible if the salary is paid by the 3PL and no employer's authority is transferred to Bolt (in conflict with article 10). {color}

{color:#ff5630}To completely minimize the risk, you could delete the detail of the repayment of the Patrol as follows: {color}

* {color:#ff5630}*Storage*{color}{color:#ff5630}:{color}{color:#ff5630} *70€*{color}{color:#ff5630}/day (Storage is agreed in advance between the 2 parties if needed) {color}
* {color:#ff5630}*Mechanics*{color}{color:#ff5630}:{color}{color:#ff5630} *2890.14€*{color}{color:#ff5630}/ month {color}
* {color:#ff5630}*Rebalancing*{color}{color:#ff5630}: {color}{color:#ff5630}*3€*{color}{color:#ff5630}/Scooter {color}
* {color:#ff5630}*Patrol*{color}{color:#ff5630}:{color}{color:#ff5630}*4.950 €*{color}{color:#ff5630}/month {color}

  

Based on the advice of the external counsel, we can conclude that we comply with Belgian law as it relates to 3PL’s employees. However, could you make the suggested change regarding the payment of the Patrol? I also attach here the emails exchanged with the external lawyer where you can consult his advice transcribed above. 

If you have any further questions, please feel free to contact me. 



Thanks a lot\! 

[^Bolt Mail - RE_ 3PL Contract [OC-OC_BE.FID66227].pdf]

