{quote}Please advice if UNIQUE index will be enough to do effective selects with filtering by campaign_id + campaign_type. If so, {{idx_dcp_ct_cid_ctype}} could be dropped{quote}

Actually, MySQL only supports DESC index in 8.0. Campaign cluster is running 5.7:
 {{(`campaign_id` }}*DESC*{{, `campaign_type`),}}

But if this was a normal ASC index, then yes, this is equivalent {{(`campaign_id`, `campaign_type`, `tag_name`)}} <=> {{(`campaign_id`, `campaign_type`)}}

