Thank you\! In this case I think it would be helpful to create a subsection in Country information → Poland → General info and country specific processes and others if needed.

As for the update requests:

[Driver Bonus Campaigns|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360021391640--Driver-Bonus-Campaigns]  - doesn’t this article apply to all/most markets?;

[Country Operational Information|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360010916439--Country-Operational-Information]:

* Address - will change as of March;
* Email - there are different emails for each city but I do not think it really matters, the tickets still get to the same queue in ZD/BH; I would add however the marketing team’s email and possibly other teams' addresses if applicable;
* Driver registration email - not sure if inserting the required city name matters in this case - to be confirmed with supply;
* Country Manager - Paweł Kuncicki is taking over on 14.02.2022, also most of the team info is outdated/incomplete;

[Country Useful Links and Channels|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360015298254--Country-Useful-Links-and-Channels] - I don’t think we are using Trello anymore; #poland_hp_team is actually #pl-hp-team, there is also #pl_cs_team channel, #fraud-pl, #poland-team-grows;

[Categories and Pricing info|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360011535314--Categories-and-Pricing-info] - at least the cancellation fee for all other categories is incorrect - it differs from city to city, OMs should have all the info;

[Airport Info|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360014009059--Airport-Info] - there are more airports we can travel to and from with Bolt, e.g. at least 2 in Warsaw; Fixed Fare sounds misleading, it seems to be the parking fee;

[Fleet Requirements and Documents|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360013852080--Fleet-Requirements-and-Documents] - last updated 2 years ago - supply can confirm if it’s still up to date;

[Driver Requirements and Documents|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360013853420--Driver-Requirements-and-Documents] - driver’s do not have to upload their work permit, not sure if the other info is correct, supply should be able to confirm;

[Vehicle and Category Requirements|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360013853120--Vehicle-and-Category-Requirements] - we accept cars made in 2000 and newer, in some cities 3 seats + 1 for the driver are enough; In Eco/Green category hybrids are accepted. Not sure why the example models are provided. Supply team should provide detailed info for this article as well;

[Scooter Info|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360013047860--Scooter-Info] - I think there are different models in different cities;

[Scooter Pricing|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360013047940--Scooter-Pricing] - not sure if it’s the same everywhere; the max trip duration changed several times, it might be different depending on the location, same with pause duration;

[Responding to the Police|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360012482920--Responding-to-the-Police] - seems ok, but since the other articles are outdated I think this one should be checked first because we actually use the info provided here and police cases are high priority;

[Driver Compensation Guidelines|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360013461400--Driver-Compensation-Guidelines] - recently due to the fact that “price too high” PRs were disabled globally and because there haven’t been manually requested PRs since last year, there was one more situation added in which the driver can be compensated. In short, we can compensate the driver if he had a cash trip costing 250 PLN or more and it did not happen or the rider did not pay. Tickets in which the driver reports such incident should be escalated by Majorel agents to those OS agents who were responsible for solving PRs. If during the price review process they would change the price of the trip to 0, they should comp the driver 25% of the price (commission charged) and advice them to cancel the receipt/contact their fleet partner to cancel it.

The procedure has been implemented so that the driver’s do not pay commission and tax on income they do not actually have. It might change in the future after the issue is consulted with local OPS team and Pricing and Billing teams.

I hope that helps, let me know if there is anything else I can do :D

