Hey\! Many thanks for looping me in [~accountid:618d2fe286c210006aa6241e]\! I believe it would be useful for the externals to understand our most common concerns. Therefore, I would advise making first questions (with respect to requirements) as specific as possible, and then add in the end, whether there are any other requirements arising out of the local regulations that we were not able to foresee while compiling the questionnaire. This would give externals better understanding of our business model.

The issues we should certainly address are as follows:

* difference in hygiene requirements of physical stores as opposed to the dark stores (as already duly noted by [~accountid:618d2fe286c210006aa6241e]);
* safety requirements (considering the visitors of our physical stores) - we do not have any contracts with visitors as opposed to pickers and other personnel, thus certain liability matters may arise;
* additional requirements to our sales areas if used as physical stores;
* requirements to the placement and storage of goods in our stores;
* additional requirements to our personnel - in terms of tools and uniforms used for work and in terms of their employment;
* additional requirements to the entrance and/or service area of  physical stores;
* additional requirements for our relationship with suppliers;
* additional requirements to insignia used to introduce or describe our stores;
* additional requirements for the sale of alcohol, tobacco and medicine;
* additional permits / licenses that need to be obtained in case of physical stores;
* additional requirements for our couriers in case of physical stores - may they enter the store while picking up the order or not etc.

I think it would be helpful for us with [~accountid:618d2fe286c210006aa6241e] to outline the main questions in a questionnaire for external counsel and let CM’s review them and supplement, if necessary. What do you think?

