Let's check the latest recorded payment from that user which had 3DS triggered for it with liability_shift: 0.

It's payment [771070621|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/view/771070621?Payment.tab=details] from {{07/02/2022, 10:53:55 UTC}}

When fraud requests 3DS, then balance send us {{/authorise}} request with force_3ds: true, and our expected behavior is:

* (/)  {{user_id: 78508902}} resolved to {{payment_user_id: 69186350}}
* (/) Order was registered in DB at {{2022-02-07 10:53:55 UTC}}
** New payment_order record created with {{id: 765509161}}
** New payment record created with {{id: 771070621}}
** New payment_row record created with {{id: 1567479901}}
* (/) In {{payment_metadata}} table store the following keys for {{payment_id: 771070621}}:
** {{force_3ds: 1}}
** {{user_present: 1}}
** {{autocapture: 1}}
* (/) authorise request was sent to Adyen at the same moment:
** request contained flags to trigger 3DS: {{additionalData.executeThreeD: true}} and {{allow3DS2: "true"}}
** response contained {{resultCode: "RedirectShopper"}} with {{issuerUrl, md, paRequest}} which means 3DS 1 was requested by Adyen
* (/) in {{user_auth_token}} table new record was created for 3DS 1 redirect token, {{id: 107000899}}
* (/) we stored 3DS 1 redirect response and {{user_auth_token_id}} in {{payment_row.token_data}} column for related {{prepare}} payment_row
* (/) we returned back 3DS 1 error response back to {{balance-user}}, which was forwarded to the mobile app at {{2022-02-07 10:53:55 UTC}}
* (/) 6 seconds later at {{07/02/2022, 10:54:01 UTC}} we got {{AUTHORISATION}} notification from Adyen with:
** {{success: "true"}}
** {{additionalData.liabilityShift: "false"}}
** {{additionalData.eci: "07"}}
** Properties in {{additionalData}} clearly shows that {{liability shift}} was not performed
* (/) We updated {{user_auth_token.liability_shift}} column from {{null}} to {{0}}
* (x) We should then reject the authorization and cancel it immediately, because we want {{force_3ds}}, but {{liability_shift}} not performed

I remember we have code to do reject + cancel, but seems it works properly [only for synchronous legacy flow|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/platform/payment/payment/main/service/paymentPrepare.ts#L490] with explicit {{checkForPayment}} step

In our case we got 3DS 1 exception at that line and we need to perform liability shift check in the authorisation notification handler.

Also for 3DS 1 case we can do it just here, [where we finish 3DS 1 authorisation|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/platform/payment/payment/main/service/threeDsOne.ts#L98-L99] with token data provided by the mobile app:

{noformat}return this.providerProxy.authenticate3ds1(ctx, authReq, (resAuth) => {
    if (Response.isNotOk(resAuth)) {
        return callback(resAuth);
    }
    const payload = this.userAuthTokenService.stringifyThreeDSOnePayload(request.payload);
    return this.userAuthTokenService.setPayloadAndMarkAsReady({noformat}

From what I saw, we only correctly handle force 3DS scenario for {{checkForPayment}} legacy flow
For balance {{/authorise}} flow it should be handled in notification handlers or in code which do final {{/authorise3ds}} or {{/authorise3ds2}} requests
Currently it's completely missing. So all balance related requests are not check liability shift status at all 🔥🔥🔥.

