{noformat} {
            "Sid": "",
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Principal": {
                "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::451613234044:role/EcsTaskRedshiftIngestionDataS3WriteLive"
            },
            "Action": [
                "s3:PutObjectAcl",
                "s3:PutObject"
            ],
            "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::bolt-redshift-ingestion-data/live/*"
        }{noformat}

Which grants the permission only to {{EcsTaskRedshiftIngestionDataS3WriteLive}}

There is no chance to get direct access to writing to S3. To make this possible, you need to use role chaining. 
I did a PR to apply the permission to assume proper role, allowing to Write to S3 bucket: 
[https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/1502/files|https://github.com/bolteu/terraform-main/pull/1502/files]

To make it work, you need to change in line: [https://github.com/bolteu/airflow/blob/d2632b4e535766b06b96e4426664b00932ecad80/src/delivery_campaigns_ab_scorecard_p_values/src/delivery_campaigns_ab_scorecard_p_values/common_functions.py#L366|https://github.com/bolteu/airflow/blob/d2632b4e535766b06b96e4426664b00932ecad80/src/delivery_campaigns_ab_scorecard_p_values/src/delivery_campaigns_ab_scorecard_p_values/common_functions.py#L366]
How you obtain the S3 client. Valid example is in the file [https://github.com/bolteu/airflow/blob/master/src/incentives_campaign_operational_metrics_supply/src/incentives_campaign_operational_metrics_supply/common_functions.py#L59|https://github.com/bolteu/airflow/blob/master/src/incentives_campaign_operational_metrics_supply/src/incentives_campaign_operational_metrics_supply/common_functions.py#L59]

On L59 (obtaining the client) and [L39|https://github.com/bolteu/airflow/blob/5d6f60002c8494866ab1aa61bb5c100b13743100/src/incentives_campaign_operational_metrics_supply/src/incentives_campaign_operational_metrics_supply/common_functions.py#L39]. The change from my PR applied + the change to construct the client shall make this work.

